\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God of the living, in whose eyes
\par Unveiled Thy whole creation lies,
\par All souls are Thine; we must not say
\par That those are dead who pass away;
\par From this our world of flesh set free,
\par We know them living unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Released from earthly toil and strife,
\par With Thee is hidden still their life;
\par Thine are their throughts, their works, their powers,
\par All Thine, and yet most truly ours;
\par For well we know, where'er they be,
\par Our dead are living unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy word is true, Thy will is just:
\par To Thee we leave them, Lord, in trust;
\par And bless Thee for the love which gave
\par Thy Son to fill a human grave,
\par That none  might fear that world to see
\par Where all are living unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O Giver unto man of breath,
\par O Holder of the keys of death,
\par O Quickener of the life within,
\par Save us from death, the death of sin;
\par That body, soul, and spirit be
\par For ever living unto Thee!
\par                          Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

